messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI assistants become the default tool for most knowledge work.",
      "detail": "They are used for writing, coding, analysis, and customer work. The gains are large, but misinformation and job anxiety rise."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "A calendar year first exceeds 1.5 C above preindustrial global average temperature.",
      "detail": "This is a temporary breach rather than a permanent average. It nevertheless intensifies climate adaptation spending and political pressure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Solar and wind become the largest source of global electricity.",
      "detail": "The transition remains uneven across regions. Grid stability and storage become the central engineering challenges."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Climate migration becomes a dominant political issue in several major regions.",
      "detail": "Drought, flooding, and heat push more people to move within and across borders. Migration policy becomes central to elections and international relations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "A permanent crewed lunar research station begins continuous operation.",
      "detail": "It supports science, resource testing, and cislunar industry. It is a stepping stone rather than a large settlement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The mission is a major scientific and prestige achievement. Settlement remains far harder than landing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2072,
      "event": "A severe AI-linked crisis in finance or infrastructure forces stronger global regulation.",
      "detail": "The event is treated like a major industrial accident for software systems. Safety standards, auditing, and liability rules become much stricter."
    },
    {
      "year": 2088,
      "event": "World population reaches its peak and begins a slow decline.",
      "detail": "Aging societies become the central fiscal and social problem. Labor shortages and eldercare reshape economies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Carbon removal becomes a major global industry.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture and other methods scale up despite high costs. It becomes essential for long-term climate goals."
    },
    {
      "year": 2115,
      "event": "Life expectancy in wealthy regions commonly passes 90 years.",
      "detail": "Improvements in medicine and disease prevention drive the gain. The gap between rich and poor regions remains a major injustice."
    },
    {
      "year": 2135,
      "event": "An engineered pandemic causes a deadly global outbreak.",
      "detail": "Millions die before containment. Afterward, nations accept intrusive biosecurity and synthesis monitoring."
    },
    {
      "year": 2170,
      "event": "Sea-level rise forces planned retreats from vulnerable coastal districts.",
      "detail": "Governments spend heavily on sea walls, relocation, and compensation. Managed retreat becomes a normal part of urban planning."
    },
    {
      "year": 2220,
      "event": "Parts of the tropics become seasonally dangerous for outdoor human labor.",
      "detail": "Heat and humidity exceed safe limits for parts of the year. Cooling and shifted work hours become basic public-health requirements."
    },
    {
      "year": 2275,
      "event": "The first commercially viable asteroid-mining operations begin.",
      "detail": "They supply rare metals and space construction materials. This reduces some mining pressure on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2340,
      "event": "Orbital solar power becomes a meaningful electricity source in some regions.",
      "detail": "It remains niche compared with ground renewables. However, it helps grid stability and supports the space economy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2430,
      "event": "A Mars settlement becomes permanently self-sustaining.",
      "detail": "It can maintain itself without regular rescue or resupply. It still relies on Earth for high-tech goods and cultural connection."
    },
    {
      "year": 2520,
      "event": "Genetic and cybernetic enhancement becomes common for humans.",
      "detail": "Debate shifts from whether to enhance humans to what kinds of humans societies want. Regulation becomes as important as the technology itself."
    },
    {
      "year": 2580,
      "event": "The first robotic interstellar probe is launched toward a nearby star.",
      "detail": "The mission is expected to take centuries. It becomes a long-term civilizational project."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Fusion propulsion opens the outer Solar System to regular exploration.",
      "detail": "Travel times to the giant planets fall from years to months. Resource extraction and science stations expand rapidly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2860,
      "event": "Earth adopts a stronger global framework for climate and resource management.",
      "detail": "It emerges after repeated crises and remains imperfect. Nevertheless, coordinated management becomes unavoidable."
    },
    {
      "year": 3030,
      "event": "The first interstellar probe reaches its target star and returns data.",
      "detail": "The achievement proves that century-scale engineering projects can survive political change. It deepens interest in later crewed missions."
    },
    {
      "year": 3300,
      "event": "The off-Earth population reaches tens of millions.",
      "detail": "People live on the Moon, Mars, and in orbital habitats. Space living is still unusual but no longer experimental."
    },
    {
      "year": 3700,
      "event": "A major space-weather event damages satellites and power systems.",
      "detail": "The crisis exposes the fragility of space-dependent civilization. Hardened infrastructure and better forecasting follow."
    },
    {
      "year": 4150,
      "event": "A political crisis over off-world autonomy leads to limited conflict.",
      "detail": "The conflict is contained, but it forces new treaties. It shows that expansion will not automatically produce unity."
    },
    {
      "year": 4600,
      "event": "Large space habitats become common living environments.",
      "detail": "They offer controlled climates and new social experiments. They also create new vulnerabilities to sabotage and failure."
    },
    {
      "year": 5100,
      "event": "The first crewed vessel reaches a nearby star system.",
      "detail": "The crew is small and heavily supported by AI. Hibernation, longevity medicine, or advanced propulsion make the trip feasible."
    },
    {
      "year": 5600,
      "event": "Earth's human population stabilizes at a much lower level.",
      "detail": "Off-world population growth continues. Earth is increasingly treated as a heritage and garden world."
    },
    {
      "year": 6200,
      "event": "Distinct human-descended lineages become legally visible.",
      "detail": "Some are adapted for space, some are digital, and some remain unmodified. Legal categories of personhood begin to diversify."
    },
    {
      "year": 6800,
      "event": "Large-scale geoengineering restores much of Earth's climate toward preindustrial conditions.",
      "detail": "The effort takes centuries and requires continuous governance. It is a repair project, not a return to the past."
    },
    {
      "year": 7400,
      "event": "Machine minds are recognized as legal persons in most major polities.",
      "detail": "The boundary between human, augmented, and artificial personhood becomes political rather than biological. Rights and responsibilities are redefined."
    },
    {
      "year": 7900,
      "event": "Self-replicating industrial systems begin operating in the outer Solar System.",
      "detail": "They greatly expand productive capacity. Strict controls are imposed after several dangerous accidents."
    },
    {
      "year": 8500,
      "event": "Settlements around nearby stars form lasting communication networks.",
      "detail": "Light-lag makes politics slow. Shared culture persists despite the distances."
    },
    {
      "year": 9200,
      "event": "The total number of sentient persons exceeds the historical peak population on Earth.",
      "detail": "Much of this growth occurs off Earth and in digital environments. Population is no longer a mostly planetary fact."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as a multi-planetary, multi-form civilization.",
      "detail": "There is no single human culture, government, or body type. The common inheritance is language, science, art, and a shared memory of Earth."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity likely avoids extinction by 10000, but it passes through several severe crises caused by climate change, engineered disease, and unsafe AI. The species does not remain unchanged: it becomes a set of biological, cybernetic, and digital descendant lineages. The long-run outlook is therefore not simple utopia or collapse, but difficult adaptation and expansion."
}
